      <pubDate>Sun, 11 Jan 2026 00:00:00 +0000</pubDate>
      <guid>https://1ronb33.au/reviews/atlantis/anemonies-to-lovers/</guid>
      <description>&lt;table&gt;&#xA;  &lt;thead&gt;&#xA;      &lt;tr&gt;&#xA;          &lt;th style=&#34;text-align: left&#34;&gt;Drink&lt;/th&gt;&#xA;          &lt;th style=&#34;text-align: left&#34;&gt;Rating&lt;/th&gt;&#xA;          &lt;th style=&#34;text-align: left&#34;&gt;Notes&lt;/th&gt;&#xA;      &lt;/tr&gt;&#xA;  &lt;/thead&gt;&#xA;  &lt;tbody&gt;&#xA;      &lt;tr&gt;&#xA;          &lt;td style=&#34;text-align: left&#34;&gt;Symbiosis&lt;/td&gt;&#xA;          &lt;td style=&#34;text-align: left&#34;&gt;3 / 5&lt;/td&gt;&#xA;          &lt;td style=&#34;text-align: left&#34;&gt;The grenadine dominates the profile as if two organisms fused into one—technically functional but the partnership feels unbalanced. I would have preferred the grenadine to contribute less aggressively. Serviceable.&lt;/td&gt;&#xA;      &lt;/tr&gt;&#xA;  &lt;/tbody&gt;&#xA;&lt;/table&gt;</description>
    </item>
    <item>
      <title>Squid Pro Quo</title>
