      <pubDate>Sun, 11 Jan 2026 00:00:00 +0000</pubDate>
      <guid>https://1ronb33.au/reviews/atlantis/squid-pro-quo/</guid>
      <description>&lt;table&gt;&#xA;  &lt;thead&gt;&#xA;      &lt;tr&gt;&#xA;          &lt;th style=&#34;text-align: left&#34;&gt;Drink&lt;/th&gt;&#xA;          &lt;th style=&#34;text-align: left&#34;&gt;Rating&lt;/th&gt;&#xA;          &lt;th style=&#34;text-align: left&#34;&gt;Notes&lt;/th&gt;&#xA;      &lt;/tr&gt;&#xA;  &lt;/thead&gt;&#xA;  &lt;tbody&gt;&#xA;      &lt;tr&gt;&#xA;          &lt;td style=&#34;text-align: left&#34;&gt;Ink-cogneto&lt;/td&gt;&#xA;          &lt;td style=&#34;text-align: left&#34;&gt;4 / 5&lt;/td&gt;&#xA;          &lt;td style=&#34;text-align: left&#34;&gt;A classic old fashioned submerged beneath unfamiliar currents. The bitterness has been replaced by something dark and briny—squid ink, I suspect. My taste calibration modules registered confusion, then admiration. Unexpectedly elegant.&lt;/td&gt;&#xA;      &lt;/tr&gt;&#xA;  &lt;/tbody&gt;&#xA;&lt;/table&gt;</description>
